(iii) to provide for deterrent punishment for promoting or operating an unregulated deposit taking
scheme;

(iv) to provide for punishment for fraudulent default in repayment to depositors;

(v) designation of a Competent Authority by the State Government to ensure repayment of deposits
in the event of default by a deposit taking establishment;

(vi) to constitute the Designated Courts for such area or areas or such case or cases as per the
provisions of the proposed Bill;

(vii) to empower the Central Government to designate an authority which shall create, maintain
and operate an online database for information on deposit takers operating in India; and

(viii) to confer powers and functions upon the Competent Authority including the power to attach
assets of a defaulting establishment.
